---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Q1 = `x ← 5
x ← x + 3
DISPLAY(x)`;

const Q2 = `print("Score: " .. 3 + 4)`;

const Q5 = `io.write("How many? ")
local n = io.read()`;

const Q6 = `DISPLAY("A")
DISPLAY("B")`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 1</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          Six questions &middot; 10 minutes &middot; Activities 1.1 &ndash; 1.6
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>
            Six exam-style questions on values, assignment and arithmetic. Some
            are written in Lua and some in{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">exam notation</b>, and nothing tells you
            which is coming &mdash; the same as in May.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Set a timer for 10 minutes.</b> Work them out on paper and do not
            run the code. Mark each answer <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b>. Guess
            rather than leave a blank; the AP exam has no penalty for a wrong
            answer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={Q1} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Exam notation" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>5</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>8</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>53</code></li>
            <li>(D) Nothing; a name cannot appear on both sides</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2</h3>

          <p>What does this print?</p>

          <Code code={Q2} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Lua" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>Score: 34</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>Score: 7</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>Score: 3 4</code></li>
            <li>(D) An error</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3</h3>

          <p><code>23 MOD 4</code> evaluates to:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>5</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>5.75</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>3</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>4</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4</h3>

          <p><code>19 / 4</code> evaluates to:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>4</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>4.75</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>5</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>3</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5</h3>

          <p>
            The person types <code>12</code>. Which of the following is{" "}
            <b>true</b>?
          </p>

          <Code code={Q5} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Lua" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>n * 3</code> raises an error</li>
            <li>(B) <code>n == 12</code> evaluates to <code>true</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>n * 3</code> evaluates to <code>36</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>n</code> holds the number 12</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 6</h3>

          <p>What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={Q6} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Exam notation" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>AB</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>A</code> and <code>B</code> on two lines</li>
            <li>(C) <code>A B</code> on one line</li>
            <li>(D) An error; <code>DISPLAY</code> can only be used once</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Hand in your six answers with <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b> beside
            each, and your time.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">The unsure marks are the useful part.</b> A
            right answer you were unsure of is a topic to revisit; a wrong
            answer you were sure of is a bigger one.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>4 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
